    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0237" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 146.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 129, of January 5, last, reporting your action in the matter of the
                    proposed extension of the French settlement at Shanghai.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that the substance of your dispatch has been
                    informally communicated to the British ambassador at this capital.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
